# Every file in this repository is owned by the design owner.
#
# With `require_code_owner_reviews` on `main`, a pull request cannot merge until
# @niravbhatt1317 approves it. One approval from any other collaborator is no
# longer enough - that was the gap this file closes. Five people have write
# access, so "one approval" previously meant any two of them could clear a
# change between themselves.
#
# Worth knowing before this puzzles someone: GitHub does not let anyone approve
# their own pull request, so a pull request opened by @niravbhatt1317 can never
# collect a code-owner approval. Those merge through the admin bypass, which
# stays available because `enforce_admins` is off. That is deliberate, not an
# oversight - it is what keeps the owner able to land their own work.

